  "landfallEstimate": "To cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a",
  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 11\nDEMS-RSMC SPECIAL TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 02.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 11 FOR NORTH INDIAN OCEAN (THE BAY OF\nBENGAL AND ARABIAN SEA) ISSUED AT 1800 UTC OF 02.11.2026 BASED ON 1500 UTC\nOF 02.11.2026\nSub: - Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu] over Westcentral Bay of Bengal off\nSouth Andhra Pradesh Coast\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d [Pronunciation: Murasu]\u201d over Westcentral Bay of Bengal moved\nNorth-northwestwards with a speed of 12 kmph during past 6 hrs and lay centered at 1500 UTC of today,\nthe 02nd November, 2026 over the same region near Latitude 14.9\u00b0N and Longitude 80.6\u00b0E, about 60 km\neast of Kavali (43243, Andhra Pradesh), 80 km northeast of Nellore (43245, Andhra Pradesh), 90 km\nsoutheast of Ongole (43221, Andhra Pradesh), and 160 km south-southwest of Machilipatnam (43185,\nAndhra Pradesh).\nIt is very likely to continue to move north-northwestwards and cross south Andhra Pradesh coast as a\nSevere Cyclonic Storm with wind speed of 100 to 110 kmph gusting to 120 kmph between Nellore (Andhra\nPradesh, 43245) and Narsapur (Andhra Pradesh, 43187), close to Ongole (Andhra Pradesh, 43221)\nduring during 1800-2200 UTC of 2nd November, 2026.\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cMurasu\u201d is under the continuous surveillance of Doppler Weather Radars at\nChennai, Machilipatnam and Visakhapatnam.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak: Cloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-\n25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very Intense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of\ndepression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-66% and HIGH:67-100%\nThis is a guidance Bulletin for WMO/ESCAP Panel Member countries. Visit respective National websites for Country specific Bulletins.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n02.11.26/1500 14.9/80.6 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n02.11.26/1800 15.1/80.3 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0000 15.6/80.0 90-100 gusting to 110 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/0600 15.9/79.8 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n03.11.26/1200 16.3/79.6 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n04.11.26/0000 17.1/79.4 50-60 gusting to 70 Deep Depression\nThe estimated central pressure is 994.0 hPa and maximum sustained wind speed is 55 kt\ngusting to 65kt.\nNellore reported mean sea level (MSLP) of 1009.7 hPa, 24 hours pressure change (P24) as -2.9\nhPa and maximum sustained wind speed (MSW) as 2900/06kt, Kavali reported MSLP of 1009.4\nhPa, P24 as -4.1 hPa and MSW 3400/09kt, Bapatla reported MSLP of 1010.9 hPa, P24 as -2.2\nhPa and MSW 200/09kt, Ongole reported MSLP of 1009.8 hPa, P24 as -2.7 hPa and MSW\n3600/09kt.\nAs per latest INSAT 3DS imagery based on 1500 UTC, intensity of the system is T3.5. Associated\nscattered to broken low and medium clouds with embedded intense to very intense convection lay\nover west Bay of Bengal (minimum CTT is -70 to -900C) and moderate to intense convection lay\nover Coastal Andhra Pradesh (minimum CTT is -40 to -700C). Scattered low and medi",
